{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"421a771abb2d8f59","type":"text","text":"Buried within this tomb is the first champion of the Storm Lord, Nordgardan. Alive during the Divergence he was a warrior selected by Normingander to protect all of goliath kind and he died in the planes of Calamity by the hands of Zariel. During that war Nordgarden was protecting Normingander while he was becoming the divine gate. In an attempt to stop him Asmodeus sent Zariel his new Arch Devil as her first task. In a battle that lasted 10 days and nights one on one Nordgardan eventually gave his life successfully holding Zariel off, allowing Normingander enough time to make the Divine Gate and seal off all the realms of the Gods.\n","x":-260,"y":-40,"width":665,"height":230},
		{"id":"996287b9af5b0e07","type":"text","text":"Exterior:\n\nJust outside Storm Crest village is a lake that flows off the side of the mountain thousands of feet below over looking it is a cliff with a perpetual waterfall with crackling electricity running through it that clears as it touches the lake. At the peak of the cliff is a stone statue of a goliath man holding a hammer, stepping on the neck of Zariel. The cliff has foot holes made of ice on its right side that lead 100 feet up and push into the water fall. A single stone plaque imbedded into the ice with the words \"Only that which is worthy may reach him\". \n\n\nIt is not possible to magically alter the waterfall in any way.\n","x":-340,"y":220,"width":745,"height":260},
		{"id":"b585e954012ed75d","type":"text","text":"Layer one:\n\nA chamber light by electricity scattering within blue walls made of ice 50ft wide in every direction. In the center of the room is an altar with the words \"Only that which was chosen may descend\" on the side of it and in the center is a rectangular hole. Once the Hammer of the All Father is placed into the it the altar will begin to glow and electricity will run through it until it reaches the floor the hammer will then float into the air and the altar will be moved back revealing a stairway below.\n\n\nDescription\":\n\nThe altar is made of Orlind stone (DC 15 hist) a blue and grey rock, all around it are symbols of an ancient language (DC 20 hist: Norsphime). In the center is a large rectangular hole at each corner a indent in the altar that reaches to the floor above the hole are the words  \"Only that which was chosen may descend\".\n","x":-377,"y":600,"width":820,"height":320},
		{"id":"83c6bd1b60354fea","type":"text","text":"Layer Two:\n\nDecent:\n\nA staircase made of Orlind stretches down past what the eye can see. Along the walls are depictions of the story of Nordgardan.\n\n1: A goliath man striking his sword through the heart of a demon with one arm push back two unrecognizable figures.\n\n2: A goliath man on one knee raising his arms to a gigantic man while a hammer floats above him. \n\n3: Two figures holding a child with a scar of lightening running down its arm. \n\n4: The same man dressed in armor standing on top a water fall with both his hands pressing into the ground beneath him.\n\n5: The God Normingander drifting into a void speaking to the man.\n\n6: A gate way made of lightening with the face of Normingander in the center, standing in front of him the same man battling Zariel. \n\n7: a snowy mountain top with blood in the snow and the same man pushing Zariel into a rift. Embedded into his chest a spear forged with hell steel with a residuum head.\n\n\nBottom: \n\nA small Orlind stone room lit by blue torch light with a single door. Above it is a plaque that says \"What is our purpose in this life.\" The answer \"To protect the ones we love or to protect the world\".\n\nThe door slides open revealing another staircase but this time you can see the bottom.\n","x":-510,"y":1060,"width":1087,"height":601},
		{"id":"5c712a8e1dbac11a","type":"text","text":"Layer three:\n\nA open chamber lit by blue torch flame, on the far wall is a tomb and in the center a table that does not look to be at the same age as the rest of the architecture. On top of it a letter.\n\nOn top of the tomb a final Plaque with that reads \"Here lays a man who would give his life for us. Prove yourself face the waters of remembrance.\" \n\nTo the left of the tomb is a cauldron of water with electricity flowing through it.\n\nSuccess on the vision:\n\nThe tomb opens reviling a dead body holding a scroll and a key.\n\nThe key is golden and is in remarkable condition. On one side etched into it written in sylvan are the words \"Find Aternis\" on the other \"Find Rae\"\n\nThe Scroll is a scroll with the Gate Spell on it. \n\n\nFailure on the Vision:\n\nYou awaken and all of you can see the room around you begin to glow a cavity in the wall opens and emerging from it is a familiar creature to some of you a Beholder \n","x":-507,"y":1780,"width":1080,"height":480},
		{"id":"81cb2412d76efc0b","type":"text","text":"Whoever plunges their head into the water will see:\n\nStanding a top a mountain side behind you a rift into the Astral Sea where the God Normingander is speaking with a Woman dressed in gold who leaves into a rift within is a monolith of gold. As you face forward you are met with the face of a fiend, bald headed with a pale white ashen face and black markings. Holding a hammer with your right arm, your left arm blown off, you see a rift start to open behind Zariel. Taking your hammer you slam it into the arch devil (Athletics DC 15) she is pushed half way into the rift. \"No matter, the day will come when we forge a weapon and break that fragile barrier. Both yours and your pitiful Gods sacrifices will be in vain.\" She then lifts her hand and you can see a ring on her finger from it a spear is summoned and plunged through your heart (DC 20: Con save). As the rift shuts you take two steps forward then fall to your knees looking down at a lake, your body falls into the snow beneath your feet and you awaken back into the room with your allies.\n","x":-419,"y":2360,"width":905,"height":313},
		{"id":"be279d23d36bdc9a","type":"file","file":"Volstarian Dynasty/Armount/Storm Crest/Images/Pasted image 20260915184153.png","x":-419,"y":2760,"width":1164,"height":740},
		{"id":"677bb9664c288dc0","type":"text","text":"[[Storm Crest.canvas]]\n#Volstarian_Dynasty ","x":-627,"y":-280,"width":250,"height":60}
	],
